# SAVESTATE relay configuration.
#
# Copy to wherever your service's EnvironmentFile points (e.g.
# /etc/savestate-relay.env) and fill in. The relay sends through a mail service
# you control, FROM that service's mailbox, with the constituent's address in
# Reply-To and CC. It never forges the sender's address, and it only delivers
# to the allowlisted committee inbox.
#
# The relay is only needed for the one-click "Send it for me" button. The site
# itself is static and works without it (the mail-app and portal buttons send
# the same letter). On GitHub Pages there is no relay; host this somewhere with
# a Node process if you want one-click delivery.

# --- where letters go (allowlist-enforced; the relay will send nowhere else) ---
RELAY_TO=SPDTCP.Committee@sen.ca.gov
RELAY_ALLOWED=SPDTCP.Committee@sen.ca.gov

# --- the From mailbox: a real address you own on the mail service below ---
RELAY_FROM=letters@your-sending-account.example

# --- outbound mail service (authenticated SMTP submission) ---
# Easiest free option: a dedicated Gmail account with a 16-char App Password
# (Google account > Security > 2-Step Verification > App passwords).
#   Gmail:    host smtp.gmail.com   port 465 (implicit TLS) or 587 (STARTTLS)
#             user = the full Gmail address, pass = the App Password
# Other free tiers:
#   Resend:   host smtp.resend.com    user "resend"   pass = API key
#   Brevo:    host smtp-relay.brevo.com  port 587
#   SendGrid: host smtp.sendgrid.net   user "apikey"  pass = API key
RELAY_SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
RELAY_SMTP_PORT=465
RELAY_SMTP_USER=your.sending.account@gmail.com
RELAY_SMTP_PASS=your-app-password
# RELAY_SMTP_SECURE is auto: "tls" for port 465, "starttls" otherwise. Override if needed.

# --- optional ---
# RELAY_SITE adds a "via <host>" line to the signature. Empty = no attribution.
RELAY_SITE=
# Leave RELAY_SMTP_HOST empty instead to fall back to a local Postfix on loopback.
